  "basis": "The task requires routing the record for the state with the highest prevalence shown on the dashboard. The legend indicates that dark red corresponds to the lowest values (near 0) and light yellow/white corresponds to the highest values (near 100). Comparing the candidate states: Rhode Island (RI) is dark red (low prevalence), Georgia (GA) is dark red (low prevalence), and Delaware (DE) is light yellow (high prevalence). Therefore, Delaware has the highest prevalence among the options and fits the 'highest-prevalence' routing criterion, while the option label 'routine monitoring' is the only available choice for that state.",
